-- title:
--   Weight-two cusp forms are cyclic over the complex Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero. The assertion is that there is a cusp form $f_0$ of weight $2$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(M)$ with the following property: for every cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(M)$ there exists an element $T$ of the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(M))\bigr)$ generated by (the underlying set of) the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) such that $T$ applied to $f_0$ equals $g$. Here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(M))\bigr)$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to the primes $\ell$ not dividing $M$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to the primes $q$ dividing $M$, the excluded set of primes being empty, so that all such $\ell$ and $q$ occur. In other words, $S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ is a cyclic module over the complex Hecke algebra of level $M$ and weight $2$, with $f_0$ as a generator.
--
--   This is the classical Atkin–Lehner–Li multiplicity-one statement that the space of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ is cyclic (equivalently, free of rank one) over the full complex Hecke algebra. It feeds into the analysis of the two-dimensional eigenspaces and the construction of bases of parabolic homomorphism spaces, being used in [`CohCarrier.nonempty_basis_fin_two_parabolicHoms_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_two`](thm.html#CohCarrier.nonempty_basis_fin_two_parabolicHoms_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_two).
-- source:
